{
  "tema": 6144,
  "slug": "no-nada",
  "titulo": "Nada: nothing, not anything",
  "subtitulo": "No veo nada.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Nada means nothing / not anything. After the verb it needs no before the verb: No veo nada (this double negative is correct). At the start of the sentence it stands alone, with no no: Nada me gusta.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Nada** = _nothing_, _not anything_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "no",
            "+ verb +",
            "nada"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "After the verb, Spanish **needs no** before the verb: **No** veo **nada**. The double negative is correct and required."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "nada",
            "+",
            "verb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "At the start, **nada** stands alone, without **no**: **Nada** funciona. It sounds stronger."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Alone as an answer: ¿Qué hiciste? —**Nada**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "An adjective after it is **masculine singular**: **nada interesante**, **nada nuevo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Handy phrases: **de nada** (_you're welcome_), **nada más** (_just, only_; _nothing else_), **nada de nada** (_nothing at all_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **no** opens the door, **nada** closes it: **no** + verb + **nada**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "No veo ==nada==; está muy oscuro.",
              "en": "I can't see anything; it's really dark."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué compraste? —==Nada==, todo estaba carísimo.",
              "en": "What did you buy? —Nothing, everything was super expensive."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Nada== me sale bien hoy.",
              "en": "Nothing's going right for me today."
            },
            {
              "es": "No hay ==nada== en el refri.",
              "en": "There's nothing in the fridge."
            },
            {
              "es": "No pasó ==nada== interesante en la junta.",
              "en": "Nothing interesting happened in the meeting."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Nada más== quiero un café, gracias.",
              "en": "I just want a coffee, thanks."
            },
            {
              "es": "No le dije ==nada== a nadie.",
              "en": "I didn't tell anyone anything."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
